---
layout: layouts/feature.njk
wide: true
title: "Apps and navigation | Shellui"
description: "Run apps built in React, Vue, Svelte, Angular, or plain HTML inside one Shellui shell. Share navigation, layout, theme, language, and dialogs."
eyebrow: Features
eleventyComputed:
  heading: "{{ mfeIntro.heading }}"
  lede: "{{ mfeIntro.lede }}"
---

{% include "framework-icons.njk" %}
{% include "mfe-intro.njk" %}

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="any-stack">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="any-stack" class="scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Built with shadcn/ui, open to any stack</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">The Shellui interface uses shadcn/ui and Tailwind CSS. Your apps do not have to. The shell shares its theme as CSS variables with the shadcn/ui names, such as <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">--background</code>, <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">--primary</code>, and <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">--border</code>. Call <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">applyTheme()</code> and the SDK writes them on your root element, with a <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">dark</code> class in dark mode.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Anything that reads those variables follows the shell when people switch theme. Pick the path that matches your app.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10 grid max-w-4xl gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6"><p class="text-sm font-semibold text-foreground">shadcn/ui</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Same token names. Your components match the shell with no mapping.</p></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6"><p class="text-sm font-semibold text-foreground">Tailwind CSS</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Point your theme colors at the variables, for example <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">bg-[var(--background)]</code>.</p></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6"><p class="text-sm font-semibold text-foreground">Anything else</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Vue, Svelte, Angular, or plain CSS: use <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">var(--primary)</code> where you want the shell color.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl">
    {% highlight "ts", "main.ts" %}
import { shellui } from "@shellui/sdk/tiny";

await shellui.ready;
shellui.applyTheme();
shellui.on("theme", () => shellui.applyTheme());
    {% endhighlight %}
  </div>
  <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground"><code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">shellui init</code> has starters for React, Vue, Svelte, Angular, Next.js, Nuxt, Alpine.js, and Tauri. Each one connects to the shell through <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">@shellui/sdk/tiny</code>.</p>
</section>

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="connect">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="connect" class="scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Connect an app in three steps</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-8 grid max-w-3xl gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
    <div><p class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary-ink">1. Add the SDK</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Install <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">@shellui/sdk</code> in the app that runs in the iframe.</p></div>
    <div><p class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary-ink">2. Call init</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">The app connects to the shell and receives its settings.</p></div>
    <div><p class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary-ink">3. Use the shell</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Show notifications, open dialogs, and navigate between apps.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl">
    {% highlight "ts", "app.ts" %}
import { shellui } from "@shellui/sdk";

await shellui.init();

shellui.toast({
  title: "Connected to Shellui",
  description: "This notification appears in the shell.",
  type: "success",
});
    {% endhighlight %}
  </div>
  <div class="mt-8 max-w-xl">{% include "feature-visual-sdk.njk" %}</div>
</section>

{# Future screenshot: Playground shell with iframe app. Add a real image here when available. #}

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="layout-modes">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="layout-modes" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Choose a layout for your product</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Set <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">layout</code> in <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">shellui.config.json</code> and every embedded app inherits it. The default is <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">sidebar</code>. Pick one below to see the shell rearrange around your app.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Size each app to 100% of its iframe rather than <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">100vh</code>, so it follows any layout. <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">windows</code> is a proof of concept and not ready for production.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10">
    {% include "shell-layouts-playground.njk" %}
  </div>
</section>
<script src="/assets/js/shell-layouts.js" type="module"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/anim-card.js" type="module"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/hero-dots.js" type="module"></script>

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="components">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="components" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Shared components, drawn by the shell</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Your app calls them through <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">@shellui/sdk</code>. Shellui draws them in the shell, outside the iframe, so they can cover the full window. Hover or focus a card to play it.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
    {% for c in uiComponents %}
      {% set wide = loop.last and loop.length % 2 %}
      <article id="component-{{ c.id }}" tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="component-{{ c.id }}-title" class="anim-card flex min-w-0{% if wide %} md:col-span-2 md:flex-row{% endif %} flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border bg-card focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary">
        <div class="p-6{% if wide %} md:flex md:w-2/5 md:flex-col md:justify-center{% endif %}">
          <h3 id="component-{{ c.id }}-title" class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground">{{ c.title }}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">{{ c.line }}</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Call <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">{{ c.call }}</code> {{ c.how }}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="anim-visual relative mt-auto border-t border-border bg-muted{% if wide %} md:mt-0 md:w-3/5 md:border-t-0 md:border-l{% endif %}" data-anim-play>
          {% include c.visual %}
          <button type="button" class="anim-play" aria-label="Play {{ c.title | lower }} animation">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" aria-hidden="true"><circle class="anim-ring" cx="20" cy="20" r="19"/><circle class="anim-ring-fill" cx="20" cy="20" r="19" pathLength="100"/><path class="anim-icon" d="M16 13.5v13l10.5-6.5z"/></svg>
          </button>
        </div>
      </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="sdk-chrome">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="sdk-chrome" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Show dialogs and notifications across the shell</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Open toasts, dialogs, modals, and drawers from your app using <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">@shellui/sdk</code>. Each call below is one line in your app.</p>
  </div>
  {% include "shell-sdk-examples.njk" %}
</section>

<section id="host-chrome" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="host-chrome-heading">
  <div class="grid items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-16">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <h2 id="host-chrome-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Theme, language, and floating actions</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">People pick theme and language once, in the shell settings. Every app reads the same choice through the SDK. App-specific actions can appear above the content or as a floating button.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">The <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">shellui init</code> starters load <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">@shellui/sdk/tiny</code>, so they connect to the shell. Add <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">applyTheme()</code> to follow the shell theme. Use the full SDK when your app also needs dialogs, authentication, or storage.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      {% include "feature-visual-chrome.njk" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# Future screenshot: Settings Appearance theme picker. Add a real image here when available. #}

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="theming">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="theming" class="scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Match the shell to your brand</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Start from a built-in theme or define your own colors with the shadcn/ui variable names. Store your theme in <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">shellui.config.json</code> or load theme files from <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">themesDir</code>.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Enable several themes to let people switch between them in Settings → Appearance. This example starts with the Shellui theme and makes two other palettes available.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl">
    {% highlight "json", "shellui.config.json" %}
{
  "theme": "shellui",
  "themes": ["shellui", "claude", "shadcn"],
  "activeTheme": "shellui"
}
    {% endhighlight %}
  </div>
  <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Apps pick up the selected colors with <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">applyTheme()</code>. The <a class="font-medium text-primary-ink underline underline-offset-2" href="{{ site.docs }}/features/themes/">themes guide</a> covers custom palettes and theme files.</p>
</section>

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="language">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="language" class="scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Keep language settings consistent</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Choose the languages available in Settings → Language. The built-in shell interface supports English and French. This configuration enables both.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Translate navigation labels and other configurable text with a <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">LocalizedString</code> object. Your apps listen for language changes through the SDK and supply their own translations. Shell layouts currently use left-to-right text direction.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl">
    {% highlight "json", "shellui.config.json" %}
{
  "language": ["en", "fr"]
}
    {% endhighlight %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="chrome-actions">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="chrome-actions" class="scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Add actions for the current screen</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Use <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">shellui.actions.set</code> to add a back button, title, or action buttons for the current screen. Shellui renders the controls and sends clicks to your app. The example below adds a back button and page title.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Update the actions when your app changes screens, or call <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">shellui.actions.clear()</code> to remove them. Switching to another app through the shell clears the previous app's actions automatically.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl">
    {% highlight "ts", "app.ts" %}
import { shellui } from "@shellui/sdk";

await shellui.init();

shellui.actions.set({
  back: { id: "back", onClick: () => history.back() },
  title: "Inbox",
});
    {% endhighlight %}
  </div>
  {# Future screenshot: Chrome actions over an iframe. #}
</section>

